# November 20, 2026: Montana, a statewide first scatter (region mt, taken by tools/choose.py --thinnest; the state had 14
# places, all in the upper Clark Fork country). Places spread from Kalispell and Glacier to Wibaux on the North Dakota line.
# Facts come from the linked sources, opened in this session: Wikipedia read as raw text (wiki_raw.py), National Register
# nomination texts from NPGallery and HMdb marker texts read with page.py, and the pages of the bodies that run each place
# (Montana FWP, the BLM, the Montana Heritage Commission, the museums, the cathedral parish, the park concessioner).
# Where no page of the managing body could be read, hours='?' and the access note says so.
